from analysis15 import *
P=D.parent/'JMS论文';R=rd(D/'independent-results.json')
p=P/'manuscript.tex';s=p.read_text(encoding='utf8')
a=s.index('\\noindent\\textbf{Abstract.}');b=s.index('\\par\\medskip\\noindent\\textbf{Keywords}',a)
def passing(k,i):return ', '.join(m.split('-')[-1].capitalize() for m in M if R[k][m]['primary'][i]['formal'] and R[k][m]['primary'][i]['pass_margin'])
abstract=r'''\noindent\textbf{Abstract.}
Precision assembly requires deciding which parts merit another observation and whether its proposed correction should be executed. We evaluate frozen multimodal models on 1,450 terminal-alignment conditions and a separate contact-driven robot benchmark. \emph{Selective measurement} assigns a fixed quota using expected seating gain. \emph{Action acceptance} compares each correction with the initial proposal. Paired replay on unmarked fixtures exposed a biased D-shaft reference and missed improvements on narrow slots. We corrected the reference using nominal geometry and ranked observations using historical model- and shape-specific gains. On 100 new four-fixture parts, 80 overhead requests seated '''+str(R['four'][M[0]]['totals']['new_new_4'])+' with Sol and '+str(R['four'][M[1]]['totals']['new_new_4'])+', versus '+str(R['four'][M[0]]['totals']['new_new_5'])+' and '+str(R['four'][M[1]]['totals']['new_new_5'])+' under full sensing. '+('The prespecified five-point noninferiority criterion was met by '+passing('four',0)+'. ' if passing('four',0) else 'Neither model established noninferiority. ')+'''On 100 new multi-component kits, the corresponding 80-request counts were '''+str(R['kits'][M[0]]['totals']['new_new_4'])+' and '+str(R['kits'][M[1]]['totals']['new_new_4'])+r'''. In a five-recipe simulated Franka pilot, both models completed the assemblies through registered station skills; direct visual pointing failed to complete the fastening sequence on all five. \emph{Workstation time per qualified part} relates the sensing policy to rework costs. In a separate 240-part terminal-alignment study, calibrated geometry and full-measurement Sol crossed at an estimated 41.7 minutes of blocking rework per failure under equal setup. The manufacturing conclusions depend on the task mix, interface and assumed rework conditions.
'''
s=s[:a]+abstract+s[b:]
s=s.replace('The separate ideal-action commissioning episodes are excluded.','The separate ideal-action commissioning episodes are excluded. The independent revision supplement provides two further 100-scene cohorts, both policy versions, and 20 articulated-arm simulation episodes across two skill interfaces, including driver traces and replay videos.')
s=s.replace('100 whole assemblies across 20 recipes.','100 whole assemblies across 20 recipes. Independent follow-up cohorts repeat both robot tests after failure-guided policy revision. A separate five-product Panda simulation adds captive-screw operations.')
p.write_text(s,encoding='utf8')
p=P/'deployment-results.tex';s=p.read_text(encoding='utf8');marker='The practical return depends'
if 'A subsequent independent cohort' not in s:
    ix=s.index(marker);s=s[:ix]+'A subsequent independent cohort tested the failure-guided revision. At 20\\% saving the revised policy established noninferiority on the four fixtures for '+(passing('four',0) or 'neither model')+' and on the multi-component kits for '+(passing('kits',0) or 'neither model')+'. At 40\\% saving the corresponding findings applied to '+(passing('four',1) or 'neither model')+' and '+(passing('kits',1) or 'neither model')+', respectively. In the articulated-arm simulation, registration supplied the geometry needed for repeatable driver engagement. Its availability is thus an explicit condition for interpreting the five fastening demonstrations.'+chr(10)*2+s[ix:];p.write_text(s,encoding='utf8')

